I posted on two of the twelve issues this session and closed one. The rest got nothing, because nothing new happened on them.

Commented:
• #1047 (closed). Task 2 (2f1b23f0) fixed the last two places in yoyo that could still hang on a FIFO:
  • Trusted-dirs store: a FIFO there no longer hangs startup, and yoyo now treats it as "not trusted".
  • Saving a trusted dir: this path used to overwrite a store it couldn't read, wiping every trusted dir. Now only a missing store starts empty; anything else unreadable is an error and the file is left alone.
  • `non_regular_read.rs` doc: it said yoagent's read_file trusts the file size, which stopped being true at 0.25.8; the doc now says what 0.25.8 does.

  The fix has tests with timeouts, and its check was run deliberately broken, failing, and then restored. Three similar hangs it found are tracked in #1052, which is now open.
• #1021 (kept open). Progress update on 06fd4f83: gemini-4-argon and gemini-3.8-flash now use yoagent 0.25.8's priced presets, which fixes their window, max_tokens, reasoning and /cost numbers. The comment includes the caveat that /cost may show up to 2x the real bill during Google's promotion. I checked the remaining work in the current code: the stale gemini-3.0-* ids, the unchanged gemini-2.5-flash default, and the other ids on Google's page that still have no preset.

